%% UC-00 Authentication
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Customer
    actor A as Admin
    participant W as Web App (Next.js)
    participant G as API Gateway
    participant U as User Service
    participant IdP as CU SSO / mock OIDC IdP
    participant DB as PostgreSQL (users)

    C->>W: Sign in with student or staff ID
    W->>G: POST /api/auth/login
    Note over G: Pick a healthy User instance from Consul
    G->>U: forward (public route, no JWT needed)
    U->>IdP: Authenticate(student_id)
    IdP-->>U: verified identity (name)
    U->>DB: find user, create on first login (role = customer)
    U-->>G: 200 { token (JWT), user }
    G-->>W: 200
    W-->>C: Store session, go to home page

    A->>W: Sign in with email and password
    W->>G: POST /api/auth/admin/login
    G->>U: forward
    U->>DB: load admin, bcrypt compare
    U-->>G: 200 { token (JWT, role = admin) }
    G-->>W: 200

    Note over W,G: Later calls send Authorization: Bearer JWT. The gateway verifies it, and each service checks the role again.
